480
00:20:38,140 --> 00:20:39,140
This kid just needs to leave.

481
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:41,140
Please trust me out!

482
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:43,140
Okay, okay, okay.

483
00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:45,140
Beat it if you got somewhere to be, guys.

484
00:20:45,140 --> 00:20:49,140
And since you all are having navigation issues, I'll act as your personal guide.

485
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:51,140
I appreciate it?

486
00:20:51,140 --> 00:20:52,140
What the heck?

487
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:54,140
Be nice to your actual students, too.

488
00:20:54,140 --> 00:20:56,140
Why would I do that?

489
00:20:56,140 --> 00:20:58,140
I can't recall you ever being nice to me.

490
00:20:58,140 --> 00:20:59,140
Huh?

491
00:20:59,140 --> 00:21:00,140
Yasuda.

492
00:21:00,140 --> 00:21:01,140
I think.

493
00:21:01,140 --> 00:21:02,140
Wow.

494
00:21:02,140 --> 00:21:03,140
Somebody who looks up to Yuda?

495
00:21:03,140 --> 00:21:04,140
I would've left to see that.

496
00:21:04,140 --> 00:21:05,140
Can't deny I would've, too.

497
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:06,140
Why?

498
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:07,140
It was boring.

499
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:08,140
Nothing at all worth seeing.

500
00:21:08,140 --> 00:21:09,140
Remy has to disagree.

501
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:10,140
Seeing you get flustered every time he called you senpai was so worth it.

502
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:11,140
That's a normal reaction to have.

503
00:21:11,140 --> 00:21:12,140
Perfectly normal.

504
00:21:12,140 --> 00:21:29,140
What isn't normal is how averse you were to simply being around this kid.

505
00:21:29,140 --> 00:21:30,140
Bad terms.

506
00:21:30,140 --> 00:21:33,140
Can't be that bad considering how comfortable the kid was.

507
00:21:33,140 --> 00:21:38,140
I didn't know he'd be here today, but he's one of my little sister's classmates.

508
00:21:38,140 --> 00:21:39,140
Huh?

509
00:21:39,140 --> 00:21:41,140
Then try and get along for her sake, yeah?

510
00:21:41,140 --> 00:21:43,140
Oh, it's complicated, Hori.

511
00:21:43,140 --> 00:21:44,140
What's the catch?

512
00:21:44,140 --> 00:21:45,140
What am I missing here?

513
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:48,140
Stop being wishy-washy and just say it!

514
00:21:50,140 --> 00:21:53,140
Is that kid possibly the one?

515
00:21:53,140 --> 00:21:55,140
He is!

516
00:21:55,140 --> 00:21:56,140
Isn't he?

517
00:21:56,140 --> 00:21:58,140
I didn't see him!

518
00:21:58,140 --> 00:22:00,140
Man, I missed out.

519
00:22:00,140 --> 00:22:01,140
Shoo.

520
00:22:01,140 --> 00:22:02,140
For real?

521
00:22:02,140 --> 00:22:03,140
No joke.

522
00:22:05,140 --> 00:22:07,140
Um, what do you mean by the one, Remy?

523
00:22:07,140 --> 00:22:08,140
I'm lost.

524
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:09,140
Same.

525
00:22:28,140 --> 00:22:37,140
둘

526
00:22:37,140 --> 00:22:45,140
Oh, I'm lost.

527
